"""
RTS24 Regulatory Reporting - Market Events Data Processing Pipeline

Orchestrates daily regulatory report generation across five market segments (EQU, ETF, FXI, WAR, BLK),

Trigger Conditions:
    - Asset-based: Waits for completion of all segment data ingestion and Saturn SLC availability
    - Manual: Accepts dag_run.conf with trading_date, processing_mode (or mode) in (load|generate_files|on_demand|replay), optional segments for load/generate_files, optional event_families for load, optional load_params for per-segment load selection, and replay filters provided either via replay_params or as flattened root-level keys (segment(s), mic_code(s), isin_code(s), participant_id(s)).

        1) Default full flow (same as load mode): load all segments/all event families, then regular generation, then on-demand checks.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14"}

        2) Load selected segments only (all event families).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "segments": ["ETF", "FXI"]}

        3) Load selected event families across all segments (list or comma-separated string).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "event_families": ["trd_order", "trd_quote"]}
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "event_families": "trd_order,trd_quote"}

        4) Load selected segments and selected event families.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "segments": ["ETF", "FXI"], "event_families": ["trd_order", "trd_quote"]}

        5) Load segment-specific event families via load_params (list of objects).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "load_params": [{"segment": "EQU", "event_families": ["trd_quote", "trd_order"]}]}

        6) Load segment-specific event families via load_params (single-object shorthand).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "load_params": {"segment": "EQU", "event_families": ["trd_order"]}}

        7) Load_params combined with global segments/event_families (merge mode: both selectors are applied and deduplicated).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "load", "segments": ["ETF"], "load_params": [{"segment": "EQU", "event_families": ["trd_order"]}]}

        8) Generate all segments only (skip load).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "generate_files"}

        9) Generate selected segments (list format).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "generate_files", "segments": ["ETF", "FXI"]}

        10) Generate selected segments (comma-separated string format).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "generate_files", "segments": "ETF,FXI"}

        11) On-demand flow only.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "on_demand"}

        12) Replay with dynamic list of optional filters.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "processing_mode": "replay", "replay_params": [{"segment": "etf", "mic_code": "WWWHHW"}, {"segment": "FXI", "isin_code": "FR000000001", "participant_id": "PART01"}]}

        13) Replay with no optional filters (one mapped generation run per supported segment for trading_date).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "mode": "replay"}

        14) Replay with single-object shorthand.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "mode": "replay", "replay_params": {"segment": "ETF", "mic_code": "XPAR"}}

        15) Replay with flattened root-level filters (without replay_params).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "mode": "replay", "segment": "ETF", "mic_code": "XPAR"}

        16) Replay with plural filter keys (segments, mic_codes, isin_codes, participant_ids accepted as aliases).
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "mode": "replay", "replay_params": [{"segments": "ETF,FXI", "mic_codes": ["XPAR", "XAMS"]}]}

        17) Replay filter values accept lists or comma-separated strings; multiple values produce a cartesian product of mapped runs.
            Input: {"trading_date": "2026-04-14", "mode": "replay", "replay_params": [{"segment": ["ETF", "FXI"], "mic_code": "XPAR,XAMS"}]}

Validation rules:
    - processing_mode: strict validation (allowed: load, generate_files, on_demand, replay).
    - segments (load/generate_files): strict validation (invalid/empty segments fail fast).
    - event_families (load/global): strict for invalid/empty values; unsupported segment/event_family combinations are warned and skipped.
    - load_params (load): strict validation per segment (invalid/empty values fail fast); accepts list of objects or single-object shorthand; can be merged with global segments/event_families.
    - replay_params (replay): strict validation for unknown keys and malformed items; replay supports list payloads, single-object shorthand, and flattened root-level filters; filter values accept scalars, lists, and comma-separated strings.

On-demand execution:
    - In default/load mode, on-demand checks run only after all load tasks succeed (ALL_SUCCESS gate).
    - In partial selected-load runs, unselected load tasks are skipped, so the load gate does not open.
    - In on_demand mode, on-demand checks run directly via the on_demand-only branch.

Replay execution:
    - In replay mode, generate_files_replay_only_flow builds mapped EMR params from replay_params or flattened root-level replay filters.
    - If no replay filters are provided, replay defaults to one mapped run per supported segment.
    - Each mapped replay run launches c_reg_8_rts24_generation and forwards only the provided optional filters.
    - On-demand group is skipped in replay mode.

Jobs:
    - Load EMR jobs per segment (EQU, ETF, FXI, WAR, BLK):
        - c_reg_2_rts24_trd_order
        - c_reg_3_rts24_trd_reject_order
        - c_reg_4_rts24_trd_quote
        - c_reg_5_rts24_trd_reject_quote
        - c_reg_6_rts24_trd_market_status
        - c_reg_7_rts24_trd_quote_request
    - Generation EMR job:
        - c_reg_8_rts24_generation

"""

